<title>USA: Maine authority $6 mln deal yields 5.7 pct in 2016.</title>
<headline>Maine authority $6 mln deal yields 5.7 pct in 2016.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Wednesday it tentatively priced $6 million Maine Court Facilities Authority rental revenue bonds at a top yield of 5.70 percent in 2016.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>MAINE COURT FACILITIES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $5,990,000*</p>
<p>LEASE RENTAL REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1996</p>
<p>BANK QUALIFIED</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: A1		    S&amp;P: AA-</p>
<p>    DATED: 10/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>10/01/1997		  190M    3.70  %</p>
<p>10/01/1998		  195M    4.00  %</p>
<p>10/01/1999		  200M    4.25  %</p>
